@startuml mcp-sequence
!include sequence.iuml
title LazyFinance — Delegated MCP Action\nIndependent OAuth consent, not first-party chat approval

actor "External MCP client" as Client <<external client>>
participant "MCP gateway / actions\n(API)" as API <<security>> #FFF2CC
participant "Private persistence" as P <<persistence>>
database "PostgreSQL 18" as DB

opt Existing-record change requires a preview
  Client -> API : action preview + MCP OAuth token
  activate API #FFF2CC
  API -> P : Owned bounded preview
  activate P #FFE6CC
  P --> API : Current selection + factual fingerprint
  deactivate P
  API --> Client : Preview context + fingerprint
  deactivate API
end

Client -> API : Execute action + stable requestId\nExpected fingerprint for existing-record changes
activate API #FFF2CC
API -> API : Verify resource, token / grant scopes\nand tool permission; normalize command
API -> P : execute(command, clientId, grantId, requestId)
activate P #FFE6CC
P -> DB : Transaction: owner lock + live grant lock
activate DB #FFE6CC
P -> DB : Recheck selection / scope / fingerprint / idempotency
alt New authorized request
  P -> DB : Domain changes + immutable receipt
else Identical request replay
  P -> DB : Read existing bound receipt; no second write
end
DB --> P : Commit one authoritative outcome
deactivate DB
P --> API : Durable result
deactivate P
API --> Client : Structured tool result / explicit rejection
deactivate API

note over Client, DB
  Write scopes default off; a read-only grant cannot execute changes.
  Create actions may omit the preview fingerprint.
  Client confirmation UX is external; conversational approval is not this authority.
end note
@enduml
